  <section class="section" id="lambda-basics">
    <h2>Lambda Fundamentals for ML</h2>
    <p>AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service that executes code without managing servers. For inference, Lambda is ideal when predictions are infrequent, latency-tolerant, or have unpredictable traffic patterns. Lambda scales automatically and you pay only for execution time (rounded to nearest 100ms).</p>

    <p><strong>When to use Lambda for inference:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sporadic prediction requests (not continuous traffic)</li>
      <li>Latency-tolerant workloads (1-30 seconds acceptable)</li>
      <li>Small-to-medium models that fit in 10GB memory</li>
      <li>Cost-sensitive applications with variable load</li>
      <li>Rapid experimentation and A/B testing</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>When NOT to use Lambda:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Real-time applications requiring sub-100ms latency</li>
      <li>Continuous high-throughput requests</li>
      <li>Large models exceeding 10GB uncompressed</li>
      <li>GPU acceleration required (Lambda doesn't support GPU)</li>
      <li>Complex orchestration with long processing chains</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Lambda Execution Environment</h3>
    <p>Lambda runs Python code in a managed execution environment. Key constraints:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Memory:</strong> 128MB - 10,240MB (increases CPU proportionally)</li>
      <li><strong>Timeout:</strong> 1 second - 15 minutes (default 3 seconds)</li>
      <li><strong>Deployment size:</strong> 50MB compressed, 250MB uncompressed</li>
      <li><strong>Temporary storage:</strong> 512MB /tmp directory (not persistent)</li>
      <li><strong>CPU:</strong> Shared across all Lambda executions in region</li>
      <li><strong>VPC:</strong> Optional ENI attachment (adds 1-2 second cold start)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout tip">
      <strong>Memory Allocation Strategy:</strong> Allocating 3GB memory gives 3x CPU compared to 1GB. For CPU-bound inference (transformers, scikit-learn), allocate 3-5GB to reduce execution time and potentially lower total cost despite higher per-second billing.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="model-deployment">
    <h2>Deploying Models to Lambda</h2>

    <h3>Packaging Models Within Size Limits</h3>
    <p>Models must fit within Lambda's size limits. Small models (under 250MB uncompressed) can be included in the deployment package. Larger models should be loaded from S3 at runtime.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">boto3</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">pickle</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">pathlib</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">Path</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">numpy</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">np</span>

<span class="cm"># Global variables persist across warm invocations</span>
<span class="va">s3_client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">client</span>(<span class="st">'s3'</span>)
<span class="va">model</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="bi">None</span>
<span class="va">model_loaded</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="bi">False</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">load_model_from_s3</span>(<span class="va">bucket</span>, <span class="va">key</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Load model from S3 (cached in memory)"""</span>
    <span class="kw">global</span> <span class="va">model</span>, <span class="va">model_loaded</span>

    <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">model_loaded</span>:
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">model</span>

    <span class="va">tmp_path</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">'/tmp/model.pkl'</span>
    <span class="va">s3_client</span>.<span class="fn">download_file</span>(<span class="va">bucket</span>, <span class="va">key</span>, <span class="va">tmp_path</span>)

    <span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">open</span>(<span class="va">tmp_path</span>, <span class="st">'rb'</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">f</span>:
        <span class="va">model</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">pickle</span>.<span class="fn">load</span>(<span class="va">f</span>)

    <span class="va">model_loaded</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="bi">True</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">model</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">lambda_handler</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Lambda inference handler"""</span>

    <span class="cm"># Load model on first invocation</span>
    <span class="va">model</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">load_model_from_s3</span>(<span class="st">'my-bucket'</span>, <span class="st">'models/classifier.pkl'</span>)

    <span class="cm"># Parse input from API Gateway</span>
    <span class="va">body</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'body'</span>, <span class="st">'{}'</span>))
    <span class="va">features</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>(<span class="va">body</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'features'</span>))

    <span class="cm"># Make prediction</span>
    <span class="va">prediction</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">model</span>.<span class="fn">predict</span>(<span class="va">features</span>.<span class="fn">reshape</span>(<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="op">-</span><span class="nm">1</span>))

    <span class="kw">return</span> {
        <span class="st">'statusCode'</span>: <span class="nm">200</span>,
        <span class="st">'body'</span>: <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>({
            <span class="st">'prediction'</span>: <span class="fn">float</span>(<span class="va">prediction</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>])
        })
    }</code></pre>

    <h3>Model Loading Best Practices</h3>
    <p>Initialize models outside the handler function so they persist across warm invocations. Load from S3 into /tmp for larger models. Cache in-memory to avoid repeated S3 downloads.</p>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <strong>Cold Start Performance:</strong> First invocation takes 1-5 seconds (cold start). Model loading happens during this time. Use provisioned concurrency or Lambda container images with pre-loaded models to warm start production functions.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="cold-start-optimization">
    <h2>Optimizing Cold Starts</h2>

    <h3>The Cold Start Problem</h3>
    <p>When Lambda hasn't executed recently, AWS launches a new container, initializes the runtime, and loads your code. This takes 1-5 seconds depending on language and dependencies. For prediction requests, cold starts add latency. For cost, they waste money on initialization overhead that doesn't process user requests.</p>

    <h3>Solution 1: Provisioned Concurrency</h3>
    <p>Keep N containers pre-warmed and ready for requests. Costs run continuously but eliminates cold starts completely. Best for predictable baseline traffic with occasional spikes.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">aws_cdk</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">cdk</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">aws_cdk.aws_lambda</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">Function</span>, <span class="im">Runtime</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">aws_cdk.aws_lambda</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">Code</span>

<span class="va">function</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">Function</span>(
    <span class="va">self</span>, <span class="st">'inference'</span>,
    <span class="va">code</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="fn">Code</span>.<span class="fn">from_asset</span>(<span class="st">'lambda'</span>),
    <span class="va">handler</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'index.lambda_handler'</span>,
    <span class="va">runtime</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="fn">Runtime</span>.<span class="nm">PYTHON_3_11</span>,
    <span class="va">memory_size</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">3008</span>,
    <span class="va">timeout</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="fn">cdk</span>.<span class="fn">Duration</span>.<span class="fn">seconds</span>(<span class="nm">30</span>)
)

<span class="cm"># Provisioned concurrency: keep 10 instances warm</span>
<span class="va">function</span>.<span class="fn">add_provisioned_concurrent_executions</span>(<span class="nm">10</span>)</code></pre>

    <h3>Solution 2: Lambda Layers and Code Optimization</h3>
    <p>Use Lambda layers to separate dependencies from code. Create a layer with all pip packages, keeping the function code small and fast to initialize. Update code without recompiling heavy libraries.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="cm"># Create layer structure</span>
mkdir <span class="op">-</span>p python<span class="op">/</span>lib<span class="op">/</span>python3<span class="nm">.</span><span class="nm">11</span><span class="op">/</span>site<span class="op">-</span>packages

<span class="cm"># Install dependencies into layer</span>
pip install <span class="op">-</span>r requirements<span class="nm">.</span>txt <span class="op">-</span><span class="nm">t</span> python<span class="op">/</span>lib<span class="op">/</span>python3<span class="nm">.</span><span class="nm">11</span><span class="op">/</span>site<span class="op">-</span>packages

<span class="cm"># Zip and publish</span>
zip <span class="op">-</span>r layer<span class="nm">.</span>zip python
aws lambda publish<span class="op">-</span>layer<span class="op">-</span>version <span class="op">--</span>layer<span class="op">-</span>name ml<span class="op">-</span>dependencies <span class="op">--</span>zip<span class="op">-</span>file fileb<span class="nm">:</span><span class="op">//</span>layer<span class="nm">.</span>zip</code></pre>

    <h3>Solution 3: Container Images</h3>
    <p>Use Docker images instead of zip packages. Compress images with DockerSlim to reduce size. Deploy pre-compiled extensions and models in image layers.</p>

    <h3>Measuring Cold Start Overhead</h3>
    <p>Track cold start times separately from handler execution to identify optimization opportunities.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">time</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>

<span class="va">init_start</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>()

<span class="cm"># Initialization code (runs once per cold start)</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">numpy</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">np</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">sklearn.ensemble</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">RandomForestClassifier</span>

<span class="va">init_time</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">init_start</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">lambda_handler</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Log timing information for cold start detection"""</span>
    <span class="va">handler_start</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>()

    <span class="cm"># Your prediction logic</span>
    <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">predict</span>(<span class="va">event</span>)

    <span class="va">handler_time</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">handler_start</span>
    <span class="va">total_time</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">init_start</span>

    <span class="kw">return</span> {
        <span class="st">'statusCode'</span>: <span class="nm">200</span>,
        <span class="st">'timings'</span>: {
            <span class="st">'init_ms'</span>: <span class="fn">int</span>(<span class="va">init_time</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">1000</span>),
            <span class="st">'handler_ms'</span>: <span class="fn">int</span>(<span class="va">handler_time</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">1000</span>),
            <span class="st">'total_ms'</span>: <span class="fn">int</span>(<span class="va">total_time</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">1000</span>)
        }
    }</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="api-gateway-integration">
    <h2>Integration with API Gateway</h2>

    <p>API Gateway provides an HTTP endpoint for Lambda functions. Clients make REST requests; API Gateway routes them to Lambda and returns responses. This creates a fully managed inference API.</p>

    <h3>Request/Response Transformation</h3>
    <p>API Gateway automatically parses HTTP requests and passes them to Lambda as events. Your function must return responses in the correct format with status code, headers, and body.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">base64</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">lambda_handler</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Handle API Gateway requests"""</span>

    <span class="cm"># Parse HTTP request details</span>
    <span class="va">http_method</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'httpMethod'</span>)
    <span class="va">path</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'path'</span>)
    <span class="va">headers</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'headers'</span>, {})

    <span class="cm"># Body may be base64 encoded for binary data</span>
    <span class="va">body</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'body'</span>, <span class="st">'{}'</span>)
    <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'isBase64Encoded'</span>):
        <span class="va">body</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">base64</span>.<span class="fn">b64decode</span>(<span class="va">body</span>)

    <span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">body</span>)

    <span class="cm"># Process request</span>
    <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">process_prediction</span>(<span class="va">data</span>)

    <span class="cm"># Return API Gateway response format</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> {
        <span class="st">'statusCode'</span>: <span class="nm">200</span>,
        <span class="st">'headers'</span>: {
            <span class="st">'Content-Type'</span>: <span class="st">'application/json'</span>,
            <span class="st">'Access-Control-Allow-Origin'</span>: <span class="st">'*'</span>
        },
        <span class="st">'body'</span>: <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>(<span class="va">result</span>),
        <span class="st">'isBase64Encoded'</span>: <span class="bi">False</span>
    }

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">process_prediction</span>(<span class="va">data</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Your inference logic"""</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> {<span class="st">'prediction'</span>: <span class="nm">0.85</span>, <span class="st">'confidence'</span>: <span class="nm">0.92</span>}</code></pre>

    <h3>CORS Configuration</h3>
    <p>Configure API Gateway to handle CORS headers for cross-origin requests from web applications.</p>

    <h3>Authentication with Lambda Authorizers</h3>
    <p>Use Lambda authorizers for custom JWT or API key validation. Authorizers run before the main Lambda function, rejecting unauthorized requests early.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">jwt</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">lambda_authorizer</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Custom authorizer for JWT tokens"""</span>

    <span class="va">token</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'authorizationToken'</span>, <span class="st">''</span>)

    <span class="kw">try</span>:
        <span class="cm"># Extract token (remove 'Bearer ' prefix)</span>
        <span class="va">token</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">token</span>.<span class="fn">split</span>(<span class="st">' '</span>)[<span class="nm">1</span>]

        <span class="cm"># Verify JWT signature</span>
        <span class="va">decoded</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">jwt</span>.<span class="fn">decode</span>(<span class="va">token</span>, <span class="st">'secret_key'</span>, <span class="va">algorithms</span><span class="op">=</span>[<span class="st">'HS256'</span>])
        <span class="va">principal_id</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">decoded</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'sub'</span>)
    <span class="kw">except</span>:
        <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="fn">Exception</span>(<span class="st">'Unauthorized'</span>)

    <span class="kw">return</span> {
        <span class="st">'principalId'</span>: <span class="va">principal_id</span>,
        <span class="st">'policyDocument'</span>: {
            <span class="st">'Version'</span>: <span class="st">'2012-10-17'</span>,
            <span class="st">'Statement'</span>: [{
                <span class="st">'Action'</span>: <span class="st">'execute-api:Invoke'</span>,
                <span class="st">'Effect'</span>: <span class="st">'Allow'</span>,
                <span class="st">'Resource'</span>: <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'methodArn'</span>)
            }]
        }
    }</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="async-patterns">
    <h2>Asynchronous Inference Patterns</h2>

    <p>For long-running predictions (>15 seconds timeout) or high-volume requests, use asynchronous patterns. Client submits request, Lambda processes in background, client polls for results or receives webhook notification.</p>

    <h3>SQS-Based Async Processing</h3>
    <p>Client puts message in SQS queue, separate Lambda processes messages from queue, results stored in DynamoDB. Client polls for completion.</p>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">boto3</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">uuid</span>

<span class="va">sqs</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">client</span>(<span class="st">'sqs'</span>)
<span class="va">dynamodb</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">boto3</span>.<span class="fn">resource</span>(<span class="st">'dynamodb'</span>)
<span class="va">table</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">dynamodb</span>.<span class="fn">Table</span>(<span class="st">'predictions'</span>)

<span class="cm"># Request submission Lambda</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">submit_prediction</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Queue prediction request"""</span>
    <span class="va">job_id</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">str</span>(<span class="fn">uuid</span>.<span class="fn">uuid4</span>())
    <span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'body'</span>, <span class="st">'{}'</span>))

    <span class="cm"># Send to SQS for async processing</span>
    <span class="va">sqs</span>.<span class="fn">send_message</span>(
        <span class="va">QueueUrl</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'https://sqs.region.amazonaws.com/queue'</span>,
        <span class="va">MessageBody</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>({
            <span class="st">'job_id'</span>: <span class="va">job_id</span>,
            <span class="st">'data'</span>: <span class="va">data</span>
        })
    )

    <span class="cm"># Store job status in DynamoDB</span>
    <span class="va">table</span>.<span class="fn">put_item</span>(<span class="va">Item</span><span class="op">=</span>{
        <span class="st">'job_id'</span>: <span class="va">job_id</span>,
        <span class="st">'status'</span>: <span class="st">'PENDING'</span>
    })

    <span class="kw">return</span> {
        <span class="st">'statusCode'</span>: <span class="nm">202</span>,
        <span class="st">'body'</span>: <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>({<span class="st">'job_id'</span>: <span class="va">job_id</span>})
    }

<span class="cm"># Worker Lambda (triggered by SQS events)</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">process_prediction</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Process queued prediction request"""</span>

    <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">record</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'Records'</span>, []):
        <span class="va">body</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">record</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'body'</span>))
        <span class="va">job_id</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">body</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'job_id'</span>)
        <span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">body</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'data'</span>)

        <span class="cm"># Run inference</span>
        <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">run_inference</span>(<span class="va">data</span>)

        <span class="cm"># Update DynamoDB with result</span>
        <span class="va">table</span>.<span class="fn">update_item</span>(
            <span class="va">Key</span><span class="op">=</span>{<span class="st">'job_id'</span>: <span class="va">job_id</span>},
            <span class="va">UpdateExpression</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">'SET #status = :status, #result = :result'</span>,
            <span class="va">ExpressionAttributeNames</span><span class="op">=</span>{
                <span class="st">'#status'</span>: <span class="st">'status'</span>,
                <span class="st">'#result'</span>: <span class="st">'result'</span>
            },
            <span class="va">ExpressionAttributeValues</span><span class="op">=</span>{
                <span class="st">':status'</span>: <span class="st">'COMPLETE'</span>,
                <span class="st">':result'</span>: <span class="va">result</span>
            }
        )

<span class="cm"># Status check Lambda</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">check_status</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Poll job status"""</span>
    <span class="va">job_id</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">event</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'pathParameters'</span>, {}).<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'job_id'</span>)

    <span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">table</span>.<span class="fn">get_item</span>(<span class="va">Key</span><span class="op">=</span>{<span class="st">'job_id'</span>: <span class="va">job_id</span>})
    <span class="va">item</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'Item'</span>, {})

    <span class="kw">return</span> {
        <span class="st">'statusCode'</span>: <span class="nm">200</span>,
        <span class="st">'body'</span>: <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>({
            <span class="st">'job_id'</span>: <span class="va">job_id</span>,
            <span class="st">'status'</span>: <span class="va">item</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'status'</span>),
            <span class="st">'result'</span>: <span class="va">item</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'result'</span>)
        })
    }</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="comparison">
    <h2>Lambda vs SageMaker Endpoints: When to Use Each</h2>

    <p><strong>Lambda is ideal for:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Infrequent or sporadic predictions with variable traffic</li>
      <li>Easy integration with other AWS services (S3, DynamoDB, SNS)</li>
      <li>Pay-per-invocation model (no baseline cost for idle time)</li>
      <li>Rapid iteration and deployment (seconds to update)</li>
      <li>Serverless architecture (no infrastructure management)</li>
      <li>Models smaller than 10GB</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>SageMaker is ideal for:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>High-throughput, continuous traffic requiring consistent latency</li>
      <li>Sub-100ms latency requirements</li>
      <li>GPU-accelerated inference required</li>
      <li>Large models (>10GB)</li>
      <li>Advanced features (auto-scaling, A/B testing, canary deployments)</li>
      <li>Built-in monitoring and model registry</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Cost Comparison:</strong> For 1 million predictions/month with 100ms processing time at 3GB memory:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lambda:</strong> ~$2,500/month (compute only, no baseline cost)</li>
      <li><strong>SageMaker:</strong> $100-200/month (ml.m5.xlarge) + compute overhead</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Lambda is cheaper for sparse, unpredictable traffic. SageMaker for continuous, predictable traffic.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="monitoring">
    <h2>Monitoring and Cost Optimization</h2>

    <p>Monitor Lambda performance through CloudWatch. Key metrics for inference workloads:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Actual execution time (includes cold start on first invocation)</li>
      <li><strong>Errors:</strong> Failed invocations (timeouts, exceptions, throttling)</li>
      <li><strong>Throttles:</strong> Requests rejected due to concurrency limits</li>
      <li><strong>Concurrent Executions:</strong> Number of simultaneous invocations</li>
      <li><strong>Init Duration:</strong> Cold start overhead (visible in logs)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
    <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">logging</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">time</span>

<span class="va">logger</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">logging</span>.<span class="fn">getLogger</span>()
<span class="va">logger</span>.<span class="fn">setLevel</span>(<span class="fn">logging</span>.<span class="nm">INFO</span>)

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">lambda_handler</span>(<span class="va">event</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Log inference metrics for CloudWatch analysis"""</span>

    <span class="va">start_time</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>()

    <span class="va">logger</span>.<span class="fn">info</span>(<span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>({
        <span class="st">'event'</span>: <span class="st">'inference_start'</span>,
        <span class="st">'memory_limit_mb'</span>: <span class="va">context</span>.<span class="fn">memory_limit_in_mb</span>,
        <span class="st">'request_id'</span>: <span class="va">context</span>.<span class="fn">aws_request_id</span>,
        <span class="st">'remaining_time_ms'</span>: <span class="va">context</span>.<span class="fn">get_remaining_time_in_millis</span>()
    }))

    <span class="cm"># Inference logic</span>
    <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">predict</span>(<span class="va">event</span>)

    <span class="va">duration_ms</span> <span class="op">=</span> (<span class="fn">time</span>.<span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">start_time</span>) <span class="op">*</span> <span class="nm">1000</span>
    <span class="va">logger</span>.<span class="fn">info</span>(<span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">dumps</span>({
        <span class="st">'event'</span>: <span class="st">'inference_complete'</span>,
        <span class="st">'duration_ms'</span>: <span class="fn">int</span>(<span class="va">duration_ms</span>),
        <span class="st">'confidence'</span>: <span class="va">result</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'confidence'</span>)
    }))

    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">result</span></code></pre>

    <h3>Cost Optimization Tips</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right-size memory:</strong> 3GB often cheaper than 1GB despite higher per-second cost (reduced execution time)</li>
      <li><strong>Use provisioned concurrency strategically:</strong> Only for baseline predictable traffic</li>
      <li><strong>Implement request batching:</strong> Process multiple predictions per invocation where possible</li>
      <li><strong>Cache models in memory:</strong> Avoid repeated S3 downloads</li>
      <li><strong>Monitor reserved concurrency:</strong> Prevent unexpected throttling costs</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

